## Comparison conventions

Rxx below identifies a numbered printed row in the corresponding FIRST page
section. Lxx is the actual one-based line in the named manuscript, obtained
with nl -ba. SAME means text/formula content matches the frozen record after
removing Markdown math delimiters, nonsemantic whitespace and routine full-width
punctuation differences. It is not a byte-equality or fresh pixel verdict.

Do not normalize away operands, signs, exponents, root indices, intervals,
point labels, omitted punctuation, or changes between comma/stop/list-separator.
Thus the punctuation differences below are explicitly retained.
Author ** emphasis is a manuscript styling wrapper; FIRST did not certify
font-weight microdetails. It neither changes the compared theorem text nor
proves source typographic fidelity.

For row comparison, the source pipeline's literal formula-break marker "↵"
represents one additional printed row. It is not part of the mathematical
expression. Two same-row captions on 0156 count once horizontally.
No production parser, KaTeX or line-audit tool was executed; row accounting is
a static comparison with FIRST, not a finalize receipt.

## Findings

D1 / operand transcription mismatch / 0158.md L13 / FIRST 0158 R08 / 469а
- Frozen source fact: y=1000000 (six zeros).
- Manuscript: y=100000 (five zeros).
- The manuscript loses one zero. This is a source-transcription discrepancy,
  not a mathematical erratum and not a reason to change 469б.
- 469б at L15 correctly retains y=-100000, per FIRST R10.
- Required source-fidelity disposition: restore 469а to the frozen 1000000 in
  a separately authorized author revision. This reviewer did not edit it.

D2 / omitted comma / 0157.md L3 / FIRST 0157 R03
- Frozen wording: "由这个方程用x表示y，并考虑到".
- Manuscript wording: "由这个方程用 $x$ 表示 $y$ 并考虑到".
- Missing comma between the y expression and 并. Formula content is otherwise
  SAME, including x=y^{2k}, y-domain [0,+infinity[, and y\geqslant0.

D3 / formula-list punctuation substitutions / 0158.md L13 and L15 /
FIRST 0158 R08 and R10 / 469а and 469б
- FIRST records the separator between y=\sqrt[3]{x} and y=\sqrt[4]{x}
  as a comma.
- Both manuscript lines use the enumeration separator "、".
- These two punctuation locations do not change the radicands or indices,
  but are not literal matches to the frozen source transcription.
- D1 and the first occurrence of D3 share L13; they are distinct discrepancies.

D4 / stop changed to comma / 0158.md L35 / FIRST 0158 R22 / 473 stem
- Frozen wording: "估计式 \sqrt[3]{x}的值。设:".
- Manuscript wording: "估计式 $\sqrt[3]{x}$ 的值，设：".
- The period after 值 became a comma. The root index3, word 设 and all three
  interval inequalities at L36 are SAME.

Summary of differences:
- Four finding categories D1-D4, covering one numeric mismatch and four
  punctuation locations (one missing comma, two changed list separators,
  one stop-to-comma change).
- No additional operand, exponent, root index, sign, named coordinate,
  interval-bracket, exercise-number, prose-word or ownership discrepancy was
  found in the requested text when compared against the frozen observations.
- Coarse figure boxes differ numerically and are documented separately below.
  They are not certified exact crops and are not silently called identical.
- Manuscript agreement does not resolve any source microdetail HOLD.

